1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:14,408
Moniq - Spending, Made Smarter.
A complete tour of the working student finance prototype. All recording data is synthetic.

2
00:00:14,408 --> 00:00:30,421
Gmail: explicit consent, read-only access
Safely disconnected recording environment. Real OAuth is tested with mocked Google responses.

3
00:00:30,421 --> 00:00:44,828
Moniq - Spending, Made Smarter.
AI-powered clarity for college finances. Isolated synthetic email demonstration.

4
00:00:44,828 --> 00:01:07,238
Accounts: one starting balance, one ledger
Register savings, link a debit card to checking, and keep credit debt separate.

5
00:01:07,238 --> 00:01:24,852
Transfers and manual reconciliation
Record completed movements without creating new income. No bank transfers are initiated.

6
00:01:24,852 --> 00:01:45,666
A paycheck email becomes a confirmed record
$10 starting cash + $400 confirmed paycheck = $410. Email extraction uses the actual parser.

7
00:01:45,666 --> 00:02:06,478
Review the purchase before it changes your balance
Merchant, amount, date, account and ML category. $410 - $15 restaurant purchase = $395.

8
00:02:06,478 --> 00:02:25,692
SmartApprove: trust requires evidence
Exact sender, account, posted status and amount caps. Automation is off by default outside this explicit test.

9
00:02:25,692 --> 00:02:41,696
Simulated automatic approval, real ledger update
The server-owned $40 dinner fixture exercises approval rules and creates an auditable transaction.

10
00:02:41,696 --> 00:03:05,706
Moniq Circles: split the bill, preserve the bank charge
$40 paid from checking. Equal split: $20 personal spending and $20 owed by Jordan.

11
00:03:05,706 --> 00:03:26,521
A repayment clears debt without creating paycheck income
Record the $20 repayment. Remaining debt: $0. Checking cash: $375; paycheck income stays $400.

12
00:03:26,521 --> 00:03:40,936
Transactions: the actual cash history
Income, purchases and reimbursements retain their original bank amounts and source labels.

13
00:03:40,936 --> 00:04:00,151
CSV imports and deduplication
Synthetic CSV only. Preview, map columns, validate, and add a categorized transaction.

14
00:04:00,151 --> 00:04:19,362
AI classification and corrections
TF-IDF with logistic regression; confidence and manual correction stay visible.

15
00:04:19,362 --> 00:04:35,365
Budgets that follow your confirmed spending
Monthly and weekly limits use your personal share, excluding transfers and reimbursements.

16
00:04:35,365 --> 00:04:54,571
Try a decision before making it
A 30-day forecast and $100 purchase scenario. Assumptions are visible; forecasts never become deposits.

17
00:04:54,571 --> 00:05:15,378
Savings goals: progress plus a plan
Record a $25 contribution and a $100 monthly plan. The estimated completion date never changes account cash.

18
00:05:15,378 --> 00:05:34,584
Answers grounded in your records
Ask about the last paycheck, savings progress, weekly spending or roommate debt. No invented amounts.

19
00:05:34,584 --> 00:05:50,588
Student deals for purchases you already planned
Clearly labeled synthetic offers, filtered by category and ranked against remaining budget.

20
00:05:50,588 --> 00:06:08,204
Subscriptions and scheduled income
Recurring-charge patterns, confirmation and upcoming payments. Confirming does not cancel a service.

21
00:06:08,204 --> 00:06:24,210
Settings and safe demo reset
Profile, goals, exports and reset controls. Only this isolated synthetic recording workspace is reset.

22
00:06:24,210 --> 00:06:38,614
Moniq - Your money. Your goals. Your financial future.
Hacklanta 2026 - Fintech | github.com/ReddyR1105/Moniq
